'''Migjorn''' ({{lang|ca|Migjorn}}, from Volisanian ''migjorn'' "midday, south") is the southernmost [[Provinces of Balboa|province]] of [[Balboa]], occupying the southern portion of the [[Balboa isthmus]] along the [[Aethiopian Ocean]] coast. It is bordered by [[Estret Province|Estret]] to the north, by [[Sinchew]] to the west across the isthmian frontier, and by the Aethiopian Ocean to the east and south. The province has an area of 30,870 km² and a population of approximately 5.8 million (2026 estimate), making it the most populous province in Balboa. The provincial capital is [[Sant Llàtzer]], a major port city at the eastern terminus of the [[Balboa Canal]].

Migjorn is the principal agricultural region of Balboa, with a plantation economy dating to the Volisanian colonial period that continues to dominate the provincial landscape. Sugar cane, bananas, rice, tropical fruits, and cacao are the principal crops, grown on large estates across the coastal plains and interior valleys. The province is also the terminus of the [[Balboa Canal]] at Sant Llàtzer, which handles interoceanic shipping and provides a significant source of revenue and employment. Tourism, centred on the Aethiopian coast and the canal city, is a growing sector. The province has a GDP of approximately $25 billion, accounting for roughly 6 per cent of national output, with a GDP per capita of approximately $4,300 — below the national average but above the poorer interior provinces of [[Tramuntana Province|Tramuntana]] and [[Nurra Province|Nurra]].

The population is ethnically diverse, reflecting the province's plantation history and its role as a destination for Fosian immigration. [[Black Balboan people|Black Balboans]], descended from enslaved workers brought to the colonial plantations, constitute the largest single group. A significant [[Fosian (Balboa)|Fosian]] community, primarily of Sinchewese descent, is concentrated in Sant Llàtzer and the canal corridor, descended from workers brought to the canal and port under the Zong Balboa administration. [[White Balboan people|White Balboans]] are a smaller presence, concentrated in the administrative and commercial centres.

